
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .gitignore — RWA-Vault monorepo
#
# Organised by category. Each section explains WHY the pattern is here, not
# just WHAT it excludes — this matters when three developers share a repo and
# need to understand which files are safe to force-add.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ─── Node.js dependencies ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Never commit node_modules. pnpm-lock.yaml is the source of truth;
# `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` in CI recreates an identical tree.
node_modules/
# pnpm's content-addressable store lives here when using `--store-dir .pnpm-store`.
# Committed stores defeat the purpose of a lockfile and bloat the repo.
.pnpm-store/

# ─── Build output ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# TypeScript emits .js, .d.ts, .js.map, .d.ts.map into dist/.
# These are derived artefacts — always regenerable from source.
dist/
# Some tools (e.g. Vite, CRA) use build/ instead of dist/.
build/
# TypeScript incremental build info — speeds up local builds but has no
# place in version control (it contains absolute paths, machine-specific).
*.tsbuildinfo

# ─── Environment ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .env files contain secrets (private keys, API keys, database passwords).
# .env.example is committed with dummy values as a template; .env is not.
# This pattern was added IN THE SAME COMMIT as .env.example — not as an
# afterthought — per production-level guidance.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# ─── Logs ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Runtime logs are machine-generated and unbounded in size.
*.log
npm-debug.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# ─── Foundry (Solidity) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Compiled contract artefacts — regenerable via `forge build`.
contracts/out/
# Forge compilation cache — speeds up rebuilds but is machine-specific.
contracts/cache/
# LOCAL Anvil (chain ID 31337) deployment artefacts are development noise.
# Testnet and mainnet broadcast logs (any chain ID ≠ 31337) are deliberately
# KEPT in version control as an immutable deployment audit trail.
contracts/broadcast/*/31337/

# ─── Rust / WASM ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Cargo build output for the pq-core native and WASM builds.
target/
# wasm-pack output directory for the browser signer build.
packages/pq-core/pkg/

# ─── Python (eval/, M11) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The venv itself is machine-specific and can be huge (jupyter alone pulls in
# 150+ packages) — eval/requirements.txt is the source of truth, regenerated
# via `pip freeze` and reproduced with `pip install -r requirements.txt`.
eval/.venv/
eval/.venv_verify/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
# Jupyter checkpoint snapshots — noise, not the notebook itself.
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ─── Docker ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Bind-mounted Docker volumes used by infra/docker-compose.yml (if any).
# Named Docker volumes (pgdata, redisdata) live inside the Docker engine
# and are not on disk here, but bind-mount patterns are excluded just in case.
infra/volumes/

# ─── OS-generated ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# macOS directory metadata.
.DS_Store
# Windows thumbnail cache.
Thumbs.db

# ─── Editor/IDE ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# VS Code workspace settings — each developer's settings are personal.
# Shared recommendations (extensions, debug configs) should go in
# .vscode/extensions.json and .vscode/launch.json and be force-added.
.vscode/
# JetBrains (IntelliJ, WebStorm) project files.
.idea/

# ─── Microsoft Office ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Office creates ~$ lock files when a document is open. These are transient
# and should never be committed. (Relevant because docs/ contains .docx files.)
~$*
